[agent:result]  |      Create a chart in the feature store.
[agent:result]  |
[agent:result]  |      Registers an HTML file as a chart in Hopsworks.
[agent:result]  |      This enables it to be used in a [`Dashboard`][hsfs.core.dashboard.Dashboard].
[agent:result]  |
[agent:result]  |      Each chart with a set `job_id` has a refresh button which triggers the job and redraws the chart once the job finishes.
[agent:result]  |      You can use this job to conviniently extract and prepare the data from Hopsworks Feature Store using its Python API.
[agent:result]  |      Once the data is acquired, it can be put into JSON to simplify the Javascript code in the HTML.
[agent:result]  |
[agent:result]  |      Note: Jobless charts
[agent:result]  |          Although charts can be created without a data preparation job, such charts are not suited to visualize data stored in Hopsworks.
[agent:result]  |          Jobless charts can be useful, for example, in case you want to display data which is already available in JSON via a REST API of an external service, or if the chart is completely static.
[agent:result]  |          Jobless charts do not have a refresh button attached to them.
[agent:result]  |
[agent:result]  |      Example:
[agent:result]  |          ```python
[agent:result]  |          # get feature store instance
[agent:result]  |          fs = ...
[agent:result]  |
[agent:result]  |          # create a chart
[agent:result]  |          fs.create_chart(
[agent:result]  |              title="My Chart",
[agent:result]  |              description="This is my chart description",
[agent:result]  |              url="/Resources/chart.html"
[agent:result]  |          )
[agent:result]  |          ```
[agent:result]  |
[agent:result]  |      Parameters:
[agent:result]  |          title: Title of the chart.
[agent:result]  |          description: Description of the chart.
[agent:result]  |          url: URL where the chart is hosted or can be accessed.
[agent:result]  |          job_id: ID of the job that prepares the data to be displayed in the chart.
[agent:result]  |
[agent:result]  |      Raises:
[agent:result]  |          hopsworks.client.exceptions.RestAPIError: If the backend encounters an error when handling the request.
