[agent:result]         data_format: If the external feature groups refers to a directory with data, the data format to use when reading it.
[agent:result]         path: The location within the scope of the storage connector, from where to read the data for the external feature group. **[DEPRECATED: Use `data_source` instead.]**
[agent:result]         options:
[agent:result]             Additional options to be used by the engine when reading data from the specified storage connector.
[agent:result]             For example, `{"header": True}` when reading CSV files with column names in the first row.
[agent:result]         version: Version of the external feature group to retrieve, defaults to `None` and will create the feature group with incremented version from the last version in the feature store.
[agent:result]         description: A string describing the contents of the external feature group to improve discoverability for Data Scientists.
[agent:result]         primary_key:
[agent:result]             A list of feature names to be used as primary key for the feature group.
[agent:result]             This primary key can be a composite key of multiple features and will be used as joining key, if not specified otherwise.
[agent:result]             Defaults to empty list `[]`, and the feature group won't have any primary key.
[agent:result]         foreign_key:
[agent:result]             A list of feature names to be used as foreign key for the feature group.
[agent:result]             Foreign key is referencing the primary key of another feature group and can be used as joining key.
[agent:result]             Defaults to empty list `[]`, and the feature group won't have any foreign key.
[agent:result]         features:
